        body: 'CDC\'s June 2026 study of travel-related cosmetic procedures (2014 to 2024) found about 145 affected US residents in 21 consultations, nontuberculous mycobacteria in 12 of 20 infection clusters and deaths in four consultations; it does not name Colombia specifically. CDC\'s Yellow Book lists bloodstream and surgical-site infection, hepatitis B and C, antimicrobial-resistant organisms, clots, fat embolism and death among the risks and tells travelers to carry English records home.',
        sourceIds: ['cdc-eid-2026', 'cdc-release-2026', 'cdc-yellowbook-mt'],
